.TH KSTAR-REPL 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-repl \- try things out interactively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar repl\fR [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
An interactive prompt: type statements or expressions and see the results.
A bare expression is printed, and names can be defined again. Inside it,
\fB:type <expr>\fR shows a type, \fB:trace M <word>\fR traces a machine,
\fB:load <file>\fR runs a file, \fB:reset\fR forgets everything, and \fB:help\fR and
\fB:quit\fR do what they say. Tab completes names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-trace-calls\fR
print every function call with its arguments, and every return with its result
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<name>\fR
the colours of drawings and of the page \fBdraw M on "w"\fR writes: auto (the default: the page follows the system, drawings are light), light, dark or high-contrast. Without it, the KSTAR_THEME environment variable or \fBtheme = "<name>"\fR in the config file (~/.config/kstar/config.toml, or %APPDATA%\ekstar\econfig.toml on Windows) decides.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<when>\fR
auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR environment variable is set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar repl\fR
start the prompt
.TP
\fBkstar repl \-\-trace-calls\fR
start it, showing every call
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
